Language: en-US
Description: Hypothesis test for isotropy in random fields observed on regular
    grids, as proposed by Baumhakel, Hörmann and Neumann (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2611.14011>. Supports multivariate and abstract (e.g.
    scalar-, but also function- or object-valued) data. Directional
    dependencies in localized structures are evaluated via an argmax
    transformation based on a standard or user-defined objective function,
    with efficient 'C++' implementations. Includes diagnostic visualizations.
